<header class="mb-6">
  <%= link_to "← Reminders", root_path, class: "text-sm text-violet-700 dark:text-violet-300" %>
  <h1 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold">Writing reminders</h1>
</header>

<section class="mb-6 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 p-4 shadow-sm">
  <p>
    Put <code>(@when)</code> on any line of a note in your folders, like
    <code>- [ ] Call the dentist (@tomorrow 9am)</code>. Lines indented under it are its notes. Check the line off, or
    tap its circle here, when it's done.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
    Without a time, a reminder goes off at 9am. Anything the app can't read is listed under “Needs a clearer time”
    rather than guessed. Changing a reminder's time reads it again from that moment.
  </p>
</section>

<% [
     ["Dates and times", [
       ["tomorrow 9am", "a day and a time, in either order"],
       ["friday", "this week's, or next week's once its time has passed"],
       ["next monday", "skips today's Monday"],
       ["Oct 21 3:30pm", "a date: Oct 21, 21 October, 10/21, 2026-10-21; next year's once it's passed"],
       ["7pm", "today, or tomorrow once it's passed; also 7:30 pm, 19:00, noon"],
     ]],
     ["From now", [
       ["in 30 minutes", "or hours"],
       ["in 3 days", "or weeks, months, years, at 9am unless you add a time"],
     ]],
     ["Repeating", [
       ["every day at 8pm", "every day, week, month, or year; also every 3 days, every other week"],
       ["every weekday", "Monday to Friday; or every monday and thursday"],
       ["every 2 weeks on tuesday", "every few weeks on a weekday"],
       ["every 15th", "days of the month; or every 1st and 15th"],
       ["every first monday", "an nth weekday; also every 2nd and 4th monday, every last friday"],
       ["every last saturday in october", "in certain months; or every 3rd saturday in jan, jun and nov"],
       ["every october 1", "dates every year; or every sep 1, dec 1, mar 1 and jun 1"],
       ["every 3 months on the third sunday", "every few months on a day of the month"],
       ["every last friday and 15th", "any of these joined with “and”"],
     ]],
     ["Starting and ending", [
       ["every day from monday", "starts on that date"],
       ["every day until friday", "ends after that date"],
       ["every day from dec 1 to dec 12", "a span of dates"],
       ["every 3 days for 3 weeks", "a length of time from the first reminder"],
       ["every year from sep 1 to sep 7", "every day of that window, every year"],
     ]],
   ].each do |heading, examples| %>
  <section class="mb-6 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 p-4 shadow-sm">
    <h2 class="mb-2 font-semibold"><%= heading %></h2>
    <dl class="divide-y divide-gray-100 dark:divide-gray-800">
      <% examples.each do |example, meaning| %>
        <div class="py-2">
          <dt><code class="rounded bg-violet-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-violet-800 dark:bg-violet-950/60 dark:text-violet-200">(@<%= example %>)</code></dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400"><%= meaning %></dd>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </dl>
  </section>
<% end %>

<section class="mb-6 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 p-4 shadow-sm">
  <h2 class="mb-2 font-semibold">Good to know</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
    <li>
      Reminders belong to whoever's folders, chosen in Settings, hold the note. A folder you both choose is shared.
    </li>
    <li>
      A time is read once, about a minute after the note syncs: “tomorrow” keeps meaning that tomorrow, until you
      change it.
    </li>
    <li>
      A couple of minutes after a reminder is found, the app ends its line with an ID like <code>^K3P9</code>, so you
      can reword the reminder or move it to another note without its time being read again. Until then, or on a line
      with more than one reminder, editing anything on the line reads the time again.
    </li>
    <li>Each reminder notifies each of your devices once.</li>
    <li>
      A reminder whose time has passed stays on its day until your overdue hours, set in Settings, have gone by. Then
      it's listed under Overdue until it's done.
    </li>
    <li>
      Marking a reminder done here checks it off in the note, adding a checkbox if the line had none. Obsidian Sync's
      version history can undo it.
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 p-4 shadow-sm">
  <h2 class="mb-2 font-semibold">How repeats move on</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
    Marking a repeating reminder done moves it to its next time. “Every 3 days” and the like count from the day it
    was done, though months and years keep to the day they started on (the 31st comes back after February);
    everything else keeps to its schedule. Marking the last one of a repeat that ends checks it off in the
    note; checking off its line in Obsidian ends it for good.
  </p>
</section>
